THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
--------------------

This licence covers the application code and the material authored for it. It
does NOT cover everything the application ships, and the terms below are not
the copyright holder's to change:

  - OpenRussian dictionary data .................. CC BY-SA 4.0
  - English Wiktionary senses (via kaikki.org) ... CC BY-SA 3.0
  - Tatoeba sentences ........................... CC BY 2.0 FR
  - Tatoeba recordings .......................... per recording; see below
  - Wikimedia Commons photographs ............... per file, CC0/PD/BY/BY-SA
  - Open-source dependencies .................... MIT and Apache-2.0

Attribution for these is a licence condition and is built from the shipped
databases' own `meta` rows rather than written down by hand, so it cannot drift
from what was actually distributed (CLAUDE.md rule 20.10). It is shown in the
app on the Credits screen and listed in docs/licensing.md.

Two of these need care before any commercial release:

  - Tatoeba recordings are licensed **per recording**, not uniformly: of the 190
    fetched, 17 are CC BY-NC, 7 are CC BY-NC-ND, and 7 state no licence at all.
    NC bars commercial use and ND arguably bars re-encoding. Build with
    `tools/build_audio.py --commercial` to leave those 31 out.
  - Photographs are filtered at harvest time to licences that permit reuse with
    credit; NC, ND and GFDL-only files are refused.

Anki decks imported by a user remain that user's own material. Bridges reads
them on the device and never uploads them.
